<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Specification</title></head><body><pre style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;">Specification# Patient Health Care System — Functional Specification

## - Observe Patient Care Enhancement through Automation of Onboarding and Collaboration Services
    - Reduce Complexity by Focusing on Core Functions

- Improve patient care through automation of onboarding and collaboration processes
    - Streamline healthcare partner integration by centralizing data exchange
    - Enhance data integrity, security, and compliance
    - Increase operational efficiency by automating routine tasks

## - In-scope: Patient Registration, Enrollment Management, Consent Capture/Validation, Partner Integration (Rationale: Key Project Functions)
    - Out-of-scope: Direct Patient Care, Diagnostic Services, Pharmaceutical Manufacturing (Rationale: Not Aligned with Project Objective)

- In-scope: Patient registration, enrollment management, consent capture/validation, and partner integration
    - Out-of-scope: Direct patient care, diagnostic services, and pharmaceutical manufacturing

## - Patient Registration and Enrollment Management (Actionable: Implement Registration and Enrollment Logic)
    - Consent Capture, Validation, and Lifecycle Tracking (Actionable: Implement Consent Management Features)
    - Integration with Internal Healthcare Systems and External Clinical Partners (Actionable: Implement Integration APIs)
    - Secure Exchange of Patient and Program-Related Information (Actionable: Implement Data Encryption Mechanisms)
    - Processing of Real-Time and Scheduled Data Submissions (Actionable: Implement Real-Time Data Processing Capabilities)
    - Exception Handling, Error Management, and Transaction Reprocessing (Actionable: Implement Error Handling Mechanisms)
    - Rapid Onboarding of New Partners (Actionable: Implement Configurable Workflows and Mappings)

1. Patient registration and enrollment management
    2. Patient consent capture, validation, and lifecycle tracking
    3. Integration with internal healthcare systems and external clinical partners
    4. Secure exchange of patient and program-related information
    5. Processing of real-time and scheduled data submissions
    6. Exception handling, error management, and transaction reprocessing
    7. Rapid onboarding of new partners through configurable workflows and mappings

## Functional Requirements

1. User interface design for patient registration and enrollment management
    2. API exposure for consent management and partner integration
    3. Encrypted data storage for patient and program-related information
    4. Real-time monitoring and alerting for consents and enrollment status
    5. Workflow management for partner onboarding and configuration

## - High Availability: 99.9% uptime (SLA: Minimal Downtime)
    - Scalability: Handle High-Volume Transactions (SLA: Minimal Latency and Efficient Data Processing)
    - Security: Data Encryption, Authentication, and Authorization (SLA: Data Confidentiality and Integrity)
    - Compliance: Regulatory and Industry-Standard Requirements (SLA: Compliance with All Applicable Laws and Guidelines)
    - Performance: Responsive User Interfaces, Efficient Data Processing, and Minimal Latency (SLA: Optimized User Experience)

- High availability: 99.9% uptime
    - Scalability: Handle high-volume transactions
    - Security: Data encryption, authentication, and authorization
    - Compliance: Regulatory and industry-standard requirements
    - Performance: Responsive user interfaces, efficient data processing, and minimal latency

## - Reduction in Onboarding Time by 50% (Rationale: Improved Efficiency)
    - Increase in Consents Captured per Day by 300% (Rationale: Increased Throughput)
    - Improvement in Data Accuracy by 99% (Rationale: Reduced Errors)
    - Compliance Rate of 100% (Rationale: Full Adherence to Regulations)
    - User Satisfaction Rating of 4.5 or Higher (Rationale: Positive User Experience)

- Reduction in onboarding time by 50%
    - Increase in consents captured per day by 300%
    - Improvement in data accuracy by 99%
    - Compliance rate of 100%
    - User satisfaction rating of 4.5 or higher on a 5-point scale

## - Increased Efficiency in Patient Onboarding (Quantifiable: Faster Time to Enroll Patients)
    - Streamlined Partner Collaboration (Quantifiable: Reduced Time to Exchange Data)
    - Improved Data Integrity, Security, and Compliance (Quantifiable: Minimized Data Breaches and Increased Compliance Rates)
    - Reduced Manual Work and Errors in Consent Management (Quantifiable: Time Savings and Error Reduction)
    - Enhanced Scalability to Handle High-Volume Transactions (Quantifiable: Scaling Capabilities for Future Growth)

- Increased efficiency in patient onboarding by automating routine tasks
    - Streamlined partner collaboration through centralized data exchange
    - Improved data integrity, security, and compliance
    - Reduced manualwork and errors in consent management
    - Enhanced scalability to handle high-volume transactions
</pre></body></html>